::3D Definition::
What does the term 3D stand for, and what are the three dimensions associated with 3D objects? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Graphics in ICT]
[tags:3d_graphics,dimensions]
{
    =Three-Dimensional; objects have Length \(X\), Height \(Y\), and Depth \(Z\)
    ~Three-Digital; objects have width, height, and color channels
    ~Three-Directional; objects can only move left, right, and up
    ~Triple-Drawn; objects are drawn on paper three times to show shadows
}

::2D Text vs 3D Text::
What is the primary visual difference between flat 2D text and 3D text? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Graphics in ICT]
[tags:3d_graphics,text]
{
    =3D text has the illusion of thickness and depth, appearing raised or standing out in space, while 2D text is completely flat
    ~2D text can be rotated and shaded, while 3D text is restricted to a single flat angle
    ~3D text is always written in capital letters, while 2D text is written in lowercase
    ~2D text is saved as a digital image, while 3D text can only exist on physical printed paper
}

::Animation definition and frames::
Animation is based on a principle of human vision where a series of static images are shown very quickly in sequence to create the illusion of movement. What is each individual still image in an animation sequence called? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Graphics in ICT]
[tags:animation,concepts]
{
    =A frame
    ~A layer
    ~A mask
    ~A keyframe
}

::Types of Animation Traditional vs 2D::
What is the primary difference between Traditional Animation and computer-based 2D Animation? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Graphics in ICT]
[tags:animation,types]
{
    =In traditional animation, each picture is drawn by hand on paper, while in 2D computer animation, flat images are created and moved using computer software
    ~Traditional animation has depth and shadows, while 2D computer animation is completely flat
    ~Traditional animation is created entirely using block coding, while 2D computer animation is drawn on paper
    ~There is no difference; both require drawing 3D models using specialized physical sculpting materials
}

