::AI definition vs standard machine::
How is Artificial Intelligence (AI) defined in contrast to standard mechanical or electronic machines? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Introduction to AI]
[tags:ai_basics,definitions]
{
    =AI is a type of computer program that can learn from information and make decisions on its own, whereas standard machines only do exactly what they are mechanically or electronically forced to do at that moment
    ~AI refers only to physical robots that can walk and speak, whereas standard machines are stationary
    ~AI is any computer program that contains mathematical multiplication operations, while standard machines do not
    ~AI refers to software programs that can run completely offline without electricity
}

::Machine Mistakes GIGO::
In the field of AI, what does the principle \"Garbage In, Garbage Out\" (GIGO) mean? 
[difficulty:easy]
[chapter:Introduction to AI]
[tags:machine_mistakes,data_cleaning]
{
    =If you train an AI model using incomplete, broken, or biased data, the model will produce incorrect or broken answers
    ~The AI program will automatically delete files from your Google Drive to clean up space
    ~AI systems are only capable of running on computers that are recycled
    ~If a computer gets physically dirty, its arithmetic calculations will contain errors
}

