::Online Meeting Drawback::
While online meetings offer several facilities such as being cost-effective and saving travel time, they also have drawbacks. Which of the following is classified as an online meeting drawback in the textbook? 
[difficulty:medium]
[chapter:Internet and ICT Environment]
[tags:online_meetings,drawbacks]
{
    =Lack of effective interaction due to the absence of face-to-face communication, which limits reading body language and emotional cues
    ~The ability to easily schedule and reschedule meetings based on convenience
    ~The option to record meetings for future reference to help participants review discussions
    ~Eliminating expenses related to travel, accommodation, and venue booking
}

::Forms Best Practices::
What is the primary rationale behind the form design tips \"use required fields\" and \"preview before sharing\"? 
[difficulty:medium]
[chapter:Internet and ICT Environment]
[tags:online_workspace,forms_etiquette]
{
    =Required fields make important questions compulsory, and previewing ensures the form is clear, correct, and professional before sending
    ~Required fields automatically collect email addresses, and previewing saves the form in Google Drive
    ~Required fields limit responses to one per person, and previewing converts the form into a quiz mode
    ~Required fields hide unnecessary questions, and previewing translates the form into regional languages
}

